{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789917886,"nonce":"Vo9TmHfjpkmKDqzPWdQVQpXWqfY=","title":"`this.m.bind(x)` and `o.m.bind(x)` call the method with shifted arguments","message":"`exc(\"t\", this.thrower.bind(5))` ran `thrower` with a garbage argument and\nraised nothing; the bare form `thrower.bind(5)` worked through a\nspecial case for a `Variable` receiver. A `MethodReference` receiver fell to\nthe generic `FunctionCall` over the method value. Fix: `lower_bind_expression`\nbuilds a `MethodCall` on the reference's receiver, spelling `this` as the\nvariable so the generated lambda captures it.","files":null}]}